        "title": "Epic and Lyric",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The most important contribution to the study of oral epic is **Milman Parry's** doctoral work (Paris, 1928) and **Albert Lord's** continuation in **The Singer of Tales** (1960). Their joint fieldwork in Yugoslavia (1930s–50s) recording South Slavic epic singers transformed understanding of Homer."
    },
