        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Epic and Lyric",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "They do NOT memorize a fixed text.\nThey generate the poem in performance using a GRAMMAR:"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-EPIC-AND-LYRIC.md#015",
      "path": [
        "02-EPIC-AND-LYRIC.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:literature:02-epic-and-lyric, git-history:literature:02-epic-and-lyric]",
        "canonical_path": "literature/02-EPIC-AND-LYRIC.md",
        "concepts": "[epic, and, lyric]",
        "current_path": "literature/02-EPIC-AND-LYRIC.md",
        "id": "maxim:literature:epic-and-lyric",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "literature",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[epic, and]",
        "section": "literature",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Epic and Lyric",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "VOCABULARY (formulae):\n  - Noun-epithet combinations for heroes, gods, places\n  - Standard phrases for recurrent actions (arming, feasting,\n    dying, sailing, arriving)\n  - Type scenes (whole narrative units with standard structure)"
    },
    {
      "id": "02-EPIC-AND-LYRIC.md#016",
      "path": [
        "02-EPIC-AND-LYRIC.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:literature:02-epic-and-lyric, git-history:literature:02-epic-and-lyric]",
        "canonical_path": "literature/02-EPIC-AND-LYRIC.md",
        "concepts": "[epic, and, lyric]",
        "current_path": "literature/02-EPIC-AND-LYRIC.md",
        "id": "maxim:literature:epic-and-lyric",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "literature",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[epic, and]",
        "section": "literature",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Epic and Lyric",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "GRAMMAR (thematic patterns):\n  - The arming scene: hero dresses in sequence (greaves,\n    corselet, sword, shield, helm, spear) — always this order\n  - The banquet scene: invitation, hand-washing, food, wine,\n    conversation — always this structure\n  - The council scene, the supplication scene, the duel, etc."
    },
    {
      "id": "02-EPIC-AND-LYRIC.md#017",
      "path": [
        "02-EPIC-AND-LYRIC.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
